From 8202b8b2876b7403fb5216ca0746d5f79949b609 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 11:49:50 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] i386-asm: runtime .code16/.code16gcc/.code32/.code64 for both
 x86 targets

GNU as switches the code mode anywhere in a file; the kernel's real-mode
code has 16-, 32- and 64-bit sections in one ELF32 object
(arch/x86/realmode/rm/trampoline_64.S, reboot.S, arch/x86/boot/pmjump.S)
and the decompressor's head_64.S starts in .code32 inside an ELF64 object.
The i386 and x86_64 assemblers now share one instruction table
(x86_64-asm.h, with OPC_NO64/OPC_ONLY64 for the forms that exist in some
modes only) and one token set, and decide at run time from
TCCState.seg_size:

 * operand size: 0x66 for 16-bit operations outside 16-bit code and for
   32-bit ones in it; the size of a mnemonic without suffix or sized
   register (ret, iret, pushf, lgdt, ljmp, cwtl, movzwl, ...) follows GNU
   as, including the .code16gcc rule that call/lcall/ret/lret/push/pop/
   pusha/popa/pushf/popf/enter/leave are 32-bit by default; moves to
   segment, control and debug registers have none
 * address size: 0x67 for 32-bit address registers in 16- and 64-bit
   code; displacement-only operands are disp16 (R_386_16) in 16-bit code,
   modrm 05 disp32 in 32-bit code and the SIB form in 64-bit code
 * rel16 (R_386_PC16) for jmp/call/jcc of 16-bit code and callw;
   R_X86_64_32 and R_X86_64_PC32 instead of 32S/PLT32 in 32-bit code of
   the x86_64 object, as GNU as relocates it
 * REX prefixes and the 64-bit registers only in 64-bit mode, the 0x40
   inc/dec forms, pusha, les/lds, arpl, bound, the direct ljmp/lcall,
   push/pop of %ds.. and the test registers only outside it
 * a lock/rep/addr32/data16 prefix written before its instruction on the
   same line is placed after the size prefixes, as GNU as does
 * same-section displacements are resolved for local symbols only;
   references to global symbols keep their relocation (GNU as behaviour)
 * 32-bit immediates are computed in 32 bits in 16/32-bit code
   ("andl $~X86_CR0_PG")
 * new mnemonics: retl/retw/lretl/lretw/lretq, pushfl/popfl/pushfw/popfw,
   pusha(l/w)/popa(l/w), calll/callw/jmpl/jmpw/jmpq, lcalll/lcallw,
   lgdtl/lgdtw/lidtl/lidtw/sgdtl/sidtl, jcxz/jrcxz, cltq/cdqe, endbr32,
   addr16/addr32/data16/data32/aword, boundl, the moffs forms a0-a3
 * the GNU as imm8 preference ("andw $0xf,%ax" is 83 /4 ib)

tccasm: the .code* directives set the mode (a .S file starts in the
target's mode; inline asm of -m16 code in .code16gcc); .word/.byte of a
symbol emit 16-/8-bit relocations; .quad takes expressions on i386;
".type name STT_FUNC" without comma (the kernel's SYM_END) and C
integer suffixes in expressions ("$0x0700a169U") are accepted.
tccelf/tccasm: the in-place addends of REL relocations are added in
the width of the relocated field (R_386_16/PC16/8/PC8).

Verified with tests/m16-check.sh: 168 .code16gcc, 168 .code16 and 174
32-bit snippets (i386-tcc), 174 .code32 and 108 .code64 snippets
(tcc, i386-tcc) byte- and relocation-identical to GNU as;
arch/x86/boot/copy.o, realmode/rm/header.o and stack.o identical to the
GNU objects; make test passes.
